{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothSiegelBound","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.RothSiegelBound","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothAuxiliaryInt","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothHouseBound","lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.RothSelection"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.exists_rothGammaFull_auxiliary","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.exists_rothGammaFull_auxiliary","kind":"theorem","line":402,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L402-L455","doc":"**All seven clauses of `Γ_m`, at the auxiliary polynomial's own height.**  Not an implication:\nthe height clause is discharged here, so what comes out is `RothGammaFull` itself, instantiated at\n`b = ⌈siegelHeight r α μ⌉` — the very bound Siegel's lemma hands step 1.\n\nThis is where the near-circularity finally closes.  `hbound` is a statement about the produced\n`H` and `N`, and `b` is a *function* of them, so neither can be a hypothesis of the existential.\nThe resolution is that the threshold `C₀^{mq}·W^{2m²q}` refers to none of the produced data — it\nis a constant of `K`, `α`, `m`, `p`, `q` alone — so it can be handed to the selection as its floor\nparameter `T` and recovered afterwards from `T ≤ H j`.  `T` is taken as a parameter above that\nthreshold rather than equal to it, because later stages impose floors of their own and the\nselection can only be given one.\n\nThe hypotheses that remain are each a fact about one fixed object:\n\n* `hfloorExp` pins `F` against `m`, `p`, `q` (the `Γ_m` exponent clause, unchanged);\n* `hm2 : 2·[K:ℚ] < 4ε²m` is the **doubled** unknowns-beat-conditions threshold, i.e. `m > [K:ℚ]/2ε²`\n  — doubled because Siegel's exponent must be ≤ 1, not merely finite, or the height is doubly\n  exponential in `Σ r`;\n* `hα` bounds the houses of the `α h` by `B`, and `hC₀`/`hW` name integers above `c K` and `4B`.\n\nNothing here mentions `N`, `r`, or the polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.hbound_of_height_floor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.hbound_of_height_floor","kind":"theorem","line":355,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L355-L399","doc":"**`Γ_m`'s height clause, from a floor on the heights.**  Everything the clause needs, reduced\nto `C₀^{mq}·W^{2m²q} ≤ H₀` — a condition the selection's own floor parameter can be set to.\n\nSo the near-circularity is fully resolved in the formal chain, not only in the argument: the\nthreshold is a constant of `K`, `α`, `m`, `p`, `q`, the selection takes it as its floor, and the\nheight clause follows. Nothing in it refers to `N`, `r`, or the auxiliary polynomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.le_pow_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.le_pow_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L345-L352","doc":"`T ≤ H₀` gives `T ≤ H₀^p` for `p ≥ 1`, so a **floor on the selected heights** discharges the\nheight clause's premise — and the selection already takes a floor. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.pow_le_pow_of_height","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.pow_le_pow_of_height","kind":"theorem","line":315,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L315-L343","doc":"**The arithmetic.**  `A ≤ C₀·W^S` with `S ≤ 2m·r₀` and `C₀^{mq}·W^{2m²q} ≤ H₀^p` gives\n`A^{mq} ≤ H₀^{r₀p}` — the height clause, from a condition on `H₀` alone. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.ceil_siegelHeight_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.ceil_siegelHeight_le","kind":"theorem","line":282,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L282-L313","doc":"**The auxiliary polynomial's height, as an integer power.**  `⌈siegelHeight⌉ ≤ C₀·W^{Σr}` for\nany integers `C₀ ≥ max(1, c K)` and `W ≥ max(1, 4B)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.hbound_of_ceil_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.hbound_of_ceil_le","kind":"theorem","line":234,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L234-L257","doc":"**`Γ_m`'s height clause, reduced to a checkable inequality.**  The clause is about\n`⌈siegelHeight⌉`, which is opaque; this replaces it by the explicit bound of `siegelHeight_le_pow`,\nso what a parameter choice has to verify is an inequality between named quantities.\n\nNothing is lost by the replacement in the direction that matters: `siegelHeight ≤ Y` gives\n`⌈siegelHeight⌉ ≤ ⌈Y⌉`, so the explicit inequality is *sufficient*.  It is not necessary, and a\nparameter family that fails it might still satisfy the clause — worth knowing before anyone reads\na failure of `hY` as a failure of the argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.siegelHeight_le_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.siegelHeight_le_pow","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L211-L231","doc":"**The auxiliary polynomial's height, explicitly.**  Combining the exponent bound with the two\nsize estimates: `siegelHeight ≤ 2^{Σr}·max(1, c(K)·(2B)^{Σr})`.\n\nTaking logs, `log(siegelHeight) ≤ (Σ r_h)·log 2 + max(0, log c(K) + (Σ r_h)·log(2B))` — **linear in\n`Σ r_h`, with every constant independent of `r`**.  That is the statement `Γ_m`'s height clause\nneeds, and the one whose absence made `hbound` look circular. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.siegelHeight_le_base","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.siegelHeight_le_base","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L169-L208","doc":"**Siegel's exponent is at most one**, and then the height is at most its base. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_prod_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_prod_pos","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L149-L167","doc":"**The condition count is positive.**  `i = 0` sits in the box with weight `0`, which is `≤ μ`\nexactly when `ε ≤ 1/2`; and the integral basis is nonempty because `[K:ℚ] ≥ 1`.  This is the one\nhypothesis of `exists_auxiliary_polynomial_int` that is not a growth estimate — Siegel's lemma\nneeds at least one equation to solve. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.two_card_prod_le_card_idxBoxF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.two_card_prod_le_card_idxBoxF","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L133-L147","doc":"**The threshold with room to spare.**  `2·deg α < 4ε²m` makes the vanishing conditions at most\nhalf the unknowns, which is what bounds Siegel's exponent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.norm_auxMatrixInt_le_house","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.norm_auxMatrixInt_le_house","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L104-L114","doc":"**The matrix bound, unconditional.**  `norm_auxMatrixInt_le` with its one hypothesis supplied\nfrom `abs_basis_repr_le`, so the arc owes nothing here.\n\nTogether with `card_idxBoxF_le_two_pow` this is the missing half of `hbound`'s non-circularity:\nboth `#box` and `‖A‖` are bounded by constants of `K` and `α` raised to `Σ r_h`, so `log b` is\nlinear in `Σ r_h`, which is what lets the `log N` cancel. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.abs_basis_repr_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.abs_basis_repr_le","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L83-L101","doc":"**The coordinate comparison, discharged from Mathlib.**  `hC` above is not an assumption about\nthe arc — it is a fact about `K`, and this is it: an integral-basis coordinate of `x` is at most a\nconstant of `K` times the `house` of `x`.\n\nThe constant is `Mathlib`'s `private c`, reached the same way `RothAuxiliary` reaches `c₁`.  Its\nvalue does not matter here; what matters is that it does not depend on `r`, `n` or `α`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.norm_auxMatrixInt_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.norm_auxMatrixInt_le","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L45-L80","doc":"**The matrix, in the same currency.**  `‖auxMatrixInt‖ ≤ C·(2B)^{Σ r_h}`, with `C` a constant\nof `K` and `B` a bound on the `house` of the `α_h`.\n\n`C` is inert in `r`, which is the point: taking logs gives `log‖A‖ ≤ log C + (Σ r_h)·log(2B)`, so\nthe matrix contributes to `log b` only through `Σ r_h` — and that is what cancels the `log N` in\n`Γ_m`'s height clause. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:MvPolynomial.card_idxBoxF_le_two_pow","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"MvPolynomial.card_idxBoxF_le_two_pow","kind":"theorem","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/RothSiegelBound.lean#L37-L43","doc":"**The box, in the budget's currency.**  `#box ≤ 2^{Σ r_h}` — the unknown count grows only\nexponentially in the total degree. ","signatureChunk":0}]}